   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 141 of the laws of 2014 amending the environmental\nconservation law relating to authorizing the hunting of big game in the county\nof Albany with rifles, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5725",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5725-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 141 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5725\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 141 of the laws of 2014 amending the environ-\nmental conservation law relating to authorizing the hunting of big game\nin the county of Albany with rifles, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nExtends certain provisions of law authorizing the hunting of big game\nhunting in Albany County with rifles.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends subdivision c of section 3 of chapter 141 of the laws\nof 2014 to extend the provision to October 1,  \n2022 2024.\n\nSection 2: effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation extends the authorization to allow for hunting big game\nin Albany County with rifles in all areas of the county except Wildlife\nmanagement Unit 4J is archery only and encompasses the City of Albany\nand adjacent populated and suburban areas.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2014: Chapter 141\n2018: Signed Chapter 160 (S.8162/A.10342)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
